<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-7962] More cases of suppressed exceptions in IsolatedUpdater</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-7962</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;IsolatedUpdater is a StreamReciever.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The contract for StreamReciever.recieve() is, @throws org.apache.ignite.IgniteException If failed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, there&apos;s a number of cases where this doesn&apos;t happen and exceptions are suppressed after being written in server log. Should replace (or augment) log.error()&apos;s with throw new IgniteException().&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;See maillist discussion.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
