                            <comment id="16413101" author="gvvinblade" created="Sun, 25 Mar 2018 17:02:18 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=ilyak&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;ilyak&quot;&gt;ilyak&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt;, changes in &lt;tt&gt;DataStreamerImpl.IsolatedUpdater#receive&lt;/tt&gt; are OK, but &lt;tt&gt;DataStreamerImpl.Buffer#submit&lt;/tt&gt; isn&apos;t expected to throw any exceptions except &lt;tt&gt;IgniteDataStreamerTimeoutException&lt;/tt&gt;. What you need to do is to finish&#160;&lt;tt&gt;curFut&lt;/tt&gt; with corresponding exception and return. It will cancel DataStreamer in a proper way.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
